00:30:03,833 --> 00:30:04,234
[SPEAKER_03]: What else?

377
00:30:04,274 --> 00:30:06,174
[SPEAKER_00]: Trying to deal with other things.

378
00:30:06,394 --> 00:30:06,574
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

379
00:30:06,594 --> 00:30:07,875
[SPEAKER_00]: So as to not have...

380
00:30:07,895 --> 00:30:09,135
[SPEAKER_03]: So this doesn't come up, yeah.

381
00:30:13,728 --> 00:30:17,270
[SPEAKER_03]: What else can a person be doing out of faith, along the red lines?

382
00:30:30,098 --> 00:30:36,862
[SPEAKER_03]: So, body's restrained, speech is restrained, the views have been upgraded.

383
00:30:39,163 --> 00:30:40,824
[SPEAKER_03]: There's the attitude of non-resistance.

384
00:30:41,795 --> 00:30:49,001
[SPEAKER_03]: In regard to the pressure, you're not just automatically trying to psychologize it, justify it, remove it, replace it.

385
00:30:50,763 --> 00:30:54,146
[SPEAKER_03]: What else can you do out of faith there, without needing to know a lot more?

386
00:30:55,687 --> 00:31:02,253
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, like, say, you're doing all this right, so what else would be there that hasn't been really... that could be addressed a bit better now?

387
00:31:05,102 --> 00:31:05,382
[SPEAKER_03]: Say it?

388
00:31:05,823 --> 00:31:06,123
[SPEAKER_03]: Thoughts.

389
00:31:06,363 --> 00:31:06,544
[SPEAKER_03]: Yes.

390
00:31:08,085 --> 00:31:08,786
[SPEAKER_03]: Yes, the images.

391
00:31:09,526 --> 00:31:09,887
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly.

392
00:31:10,267 --> 00:31:14,451
[SPEAKER_03]: Okay, I do have a say in what I choose to revolve around.

393
00:31:15,052 --> 00:31:26,103
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, images present themselves, in the same sense possibilities for physical actions or verbal actions present themselves, but then you choose to engage and revolve, feed and cultivate.

394
00:31:26,123 --> 00:31:27,785
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it's like, okay, so I will not then

395
00:31:29,363 --> 00:31:35,829
[SPEAKER_03]: Feed the unsuitable images that are rooted in lust, or anger, or cruelty, you know, so to say.

396
00:31:36,650 --> 00:31:41,234
[SPEAKER_03]: Or, then later, conceit, belonging to a clan, and so on.

397
00:31:41,354 --> 00:31:42,135
[SPEAKER_03]: The subtler ones.

398
00:31:42,355 --> 00:31:43,176
[SPEAKER_01]: I just won't feed them.

399
00:31:44,377 --> 00:31:50,403
[SPEAKER_03]: I will not give more momentum to them when they present themselves.

400
00:31:50,423 --> 00:31:51,844
[SPEAKER_03]: I'm not blaming them for the problem.

401
00:31:53,118 --> 00:31:59,159
[SPEAKER_03]: I am unresisting the pressure, but I could also not, just habitually not... Give them attention.

402
00:31:59,419 --> 00:32:01,940
[SPEAKER_03]: Give them, yeah, give them unsuitable attention, basically.

403
00:32:02,100 --> 00:32:02,540
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

404
00:32:02,740 --> 00:32:03,500
[SPEAKER_03]: Center stage.

405
00:32:03,740 --> 00:32:05,221
[SPEAKER_03]: Center stage, we said before, yeah.

406
00:32:05,261 --> 00:32:06,701
[SPEAKER_03]: Don't allow them in the center stage.

407
00:32:06,821 --> 00:32:09,082
[SPEAKER_03]: Let them be there, but don't allow them in the center stage.

408
00:32:12,623 --> 00:32:18,704
[SPEAKER_03]: What else can you do, then, out of faith, that can then tame the animal even further?

409
00:32:22,417 --> 00:32:25,159
[SPEAKER_03]: Presented with certain images.

410
00:32:26,280 --> 00:32:27,241
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, exactly.

411
00:32:28,021 --> 00:32:33,986
[SPEAKER_03]: Start, start basically inducing certain context for it, because you know, okay, it sees me.

412
00:32:35,006 --> 00:32:41,311
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, let me think about these things of this kind, so that it will reflect back onto that animal.

413
00:32:41,791 --> 00:32:44,013
[SPEAKER_03]: Those perceptions, whatever perceptions.

414
00:32:44,133 --> 00:32:45,814
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, the perceptions.

415
00:32:46,235 --> 00:32:50,378
[SPEAKER_03]: Anicca, un-unability, non-resistance,

416
00:32:51,250 --> 00:32:56,531
[SPEAKER_03]: The perceptions of non-resistance that would then establish the animal in the state of metta, basically.

417
00:32:58,072 --> 00:33:00,713
[SPEAKER_03]: As we said before, it's the animal that practices metta, not you.

418
00:33:01,073 --> 00:33:02,373
[SPEAKER_03]: You're just setting it up for it.

419
00:33:03,353 --> 00:33:05,714
[SPEAKER_03]: Mind you, it's the animal that practices samādhi, not you.

420
00:33:06,514 --> 00:33:09,695
[SPEAKER_03]: It's citta in samādhi, not... it's not your thing that you're doing.

421
00:33:10,695 --> 00:33:13,096
[SPEAKER_03]: So, that's how you're unifying the animal as well.

422
00:33:13,116 --> 00:33:14,256
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

423
00:33:14,336 --> 00:33:15,157
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, I'm doing the samādhi.

424
00:33:15,197 --> 00:33:15,457
[SPEAKER_03]: No, no, no.

425
00:33:15,477 --> 00:33:19,738
[SPEAKER_03]: You can only be setting it up rightly through the indirect means, through mindfulness,

426
00:33:20,332 --> 00:33:25,794
[SPEAKER_03]: Correctly, peripherally, discerning stuff, so that then the animal is unified, elevated.

427
00:33:27,455 --> 00:33:28,215
[SPEAKER_01]: What else could you do?

428
00:33:28,255 --> 00:33:29,055
[SPEAKER_03]: Have faith, then.

429
00:33:30,095 --> 00:33:42,440
[SPEAKER_03]: So, presenting with suitable contexts, right contemplations, on the basis of non-resistance, on the basis of virtual solitude, on the basis of uninterrupted virtue and restraint.

430
00:33:44,881 --> 00:33:45,721
[SPEAKER_01]: What else can you do?

431
00:33:49,236 --> 00:33:54,761
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you talk to it directly now, since there is nothing else in between obscuring the communication?

432
00:33:56,602 --> 00:33:58,504
[SPEAKER_03]: Can you tell it to calm down if it's agitated?

433
00:34:01,826 --> 00:34:02,147
[SPEAKER_01]: You can.

434
00:34:02,287 --> 00:34:02,967
[SPEAKER_03]: You always could.

435
00:34:03,388 --> 00:34:07,231
[SPEAKER_03]: It's just that it didn't listen before, because it wasn't taking it seriously enough.

436
00:34:08,912 --> 00:34:18,040
[SPEAKER_03]: But now that you would have purified your body language, verbal language, mental language that this animal is reading, now it's solely focused onto you, and now when you

437
00:34:18,753 --> 00:34:20,114
[SPEAKER_03]: Tell it, it actually hears you.

438
00:34:22,877 --> 00:34:24,018
[SPEAKER_03]: And then you tell it to calm down.

439
00:34:26,720 --> 00:34:28,281
[SPEAKER_03]: You tell it to relinquish.

440
00:34:29,102 --> 00:34:30,223
[SPEAKER_03]: You tell it to let go.

441
00:34:31,664 --> 00:34:32,045
[SPEAKER_01]: And it will.

442
00:34:42,179 --> 00:34:45,041
[SPEAKER_03]: So, is there anything else that the person on the face would need to do?

443
00:34:46,322 --> 00:34:49,024
[SPEAKER_03]: I'd say, not much.

444
00:35:00,293 --> 00:35:02,895
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's like... depends.

445
00:35:02,955 --> 00:35:08,159
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, we already said, presented with certain contexts that would be on the level of like...

446
00:35:11,232 --> 00:35:13,293
[SPEAKER_00]: Calming it further or unifying it.

447
00:35:13,933 --> 00:35:29,782
[SPEAKER_00]: But then there's also, like you were saying, I think, one or two talks ago, like presenting it with the, like with the wild elephant, you would sort of show it the the spears or show it the the the things that like...

448
00:35:30,022 --> 00:35:30,963
[SPEAKER_03]: When would you do that?

449
00:35:31,603 --> 00:35:33,464
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't even specify that back then.

450
00:35:34,705 --> 00:35:39,747
[SPEAKER_03]: So, like, just now we described, like, this gradual training.

451
00:35:43,512 --> 00:36:01,616
[SPEAKER_03]: When would you know to present the agitating context, or possibly agitating context, to see if there is agitation in the animal, or presented the non-agitating context?

452
00:36:01,756 --> 00:36:05,477
[SPEAKER_03]: What would be the criteria for that?

453
00:36:06,017 --> 00:36:10,718
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, let's say one obvious one is if it's agitated already, then you don't need to present a bit more.

454
00:36:10,738 --> 00:36:12,559
[SPEAKER_03]: How do you know it's agitated already?

455
00:36:13,632 --> 00:36:15,814
[SPEAKER_03]: How are you measuring animal's agitation?

456
00:36:21,959 --> 00:36:22,479
[SPEAKER_02]: Suffering.

457
00:36:27,203 --> 00:36:27,864
[SPEAKER_03]: Suffering.

458
00:36:28,324 --> 00:36:28,845
[SPEAKER_00]: Acting out.

459
00:36:29,865 --> 00:36:30,426
[SPEAKER_03]: Acting out.

460
00:36:31,547 --> 00:36:32,047
[SPEAKER_00]: Pressure.

461
00:36:32,488 --> 00:36:33,368
[SPEAKER_00]: Being pressured.

462
00:36:36,411 --> 00:36:36,691
[SPEAKER_01]: Pressure.

463
00:36:36,711 --> 00:36:38,353
[SPEAKER_01]: The emotional outbursts.

464
00:36:39,493 --> 00:36:42,336
[SPEAKER_03]: No, this would be, like, way too coarse now for this.

465
00:36:43,277 --> 00:36:47,878
[SPEAKER_03]: All of those pretty much... subtler, subtler than all of that.

466
00:36:51,119 --> 00:36:56,820
[SPEAKER_03]: It's kind of where the pressure is, but... it's always some pressure, I suppose.

467
00:36:58,781 --> 00:37:01,341
[SPEAKER_03]: It's not necessarily going to be... What?

468
00:37:03,962 --> 00:37:04,182
[SPEAKER_03]: What?

469
00:37:04,682 --> 00:37:05,862
[SPEAKER_03]: What do you do in regard to pressure?

470
00:37:05,882 --> 00:37:07,483
[SPEAKER_03]: What's the first thing you do in regard to pressure?

471
00:37:07,523 --> 00:37:08,743
[SPEAKER_03]: What did you say you should stop doing?

472
00:37:09,083 --> 00:37:09,583
[SPEAKER_00]: Resistance.

473
00:37:09,943 --> 00:37:11,124
[SPEAKER_03]: Resistance, yeah.

474
00:37:11,144 --> 00:37:12,384
[SPEAKER_03]: So, if there is resistance,

475
00:37:14,934 --> 00:37:22,581
[SPEAKER_03]: If it's not sufficiently unresisted, then you shouldn't be agitating it, because you're just gonna tighten the resistance.

476
00:37:23,702 --> 00:37:30,487
[SPEAKER_03]: So, that's why you first have to unresist the degree of perceived, felt, experienced resistance.

477
00:37:30,928 --> 00:37:31,188
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

478
00:37:33,189 --> 00:37:42,177
[SPEAKER_00]: I guess there, yeah, there has to be, like, also, I mean, the other possible answer, I suppose, could be, like, when you know that now you can kind of talk to it directly.

479
00:37:42,873 --> 00:37:50,437
[SPEAKER_00]: Because there has to be kind of a degree of confidence that, you know, you can tell it to calm down.

480
00:37:50,637 --> 00:37:53,199
[SPEAKER_00]: You show it something, it might start to get agitated, and it will...

481
00:37:53,239 --> 00:37:53,479
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

482
00:37:53,499 --> 00:37:54,059
[SPEAKER_00]: You can calm it down.

483
00:37:54,079 --> 00:37:54,659
[SPEAKER_03]: You can calm it down.

484
00:37:55,040 --> 00:38:04,725
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, that's why the importance of gradual training, not like people just hearing the end part of the gradual training and then just trying to apply that right now, so I can get quicker there.

485
00:38:05,750 --> 00:38:10,072
[SPEAKER_03]: It's like you have no criteria for whether the animal is being agitated or not.

486
00:38:10,112 --> 00:38:12,893
[SPEAKER_03]: You're just throwing these things that can obviously make it worse.

487
00:38:14,714 --> 00:38:23,138
[SPEAKER_03]: But see, the whole point is, like, it will constrict to some extent when you present it with things that it doesn't want to see.

488
00:38:24,479 --> 00:38:30,862
[SPEAKER_03]: So you want to unconstrict it first, so that when it constricts back, it's just still on the neutral level.

489
00:38:32,601 --> 00:38:36,142
[SPEAKER_03]: But if it's already constricted, there's some resistance there.

490
00:38:38,382 --> 00:38:41,103
[SPEAKER_03]: Presenting with more is just not going to be balanced.

491
00:38:42,463 --> 00:38:58,167
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's why even when the Buddha was teaching first-time people, they would come, he would always talk first about benefits, you know, virtue, heavens, rebirth, great rewards, all of that, which is kind of, oh, wow, you know, great.

492
00:38:59,104 --> 00:39:07,992
[SPEAKER_03]: And it unconstricts more, and more, and more, and then he tells them about the peril, degradation of sensuality, and so on, impermanence, and all of that.

493
00:39:08,313 --> 00:39:14,078
[SPEAKER_03]: So, there's immediate constriction, but their starting point has been widened, so to speak.

494
00:39:14,799 --> 00:39:19,943
[SPEAKER_03]: So, when they constrict back, they're going to constrict onto the middle, not too narrow.

495
00:39:21,925 --> 00:39:23,507
[SPEAKER_03]: Obviously, you know, the Buddha could see that.

496
00:39:24,714 --> 00:39:39,027
[SPEAKER_03]: Clearly, in regard to the others, but you could safely know that if there is resistance, and now you're presenting these agitating contexts of impermanence, mindfulness of death,

497
00:39:40,956 --> 00:39:48,423
[SPEAKER_03]: Disgust and all of that to the mind, without unresisting it first, it's probably going to be rooted in resistance.

498
00:39:48,643 --> 00:39:52,266
[SPEAKER_03]: You're trying to get rid of it by feeding this to go away quicker, to stop doing it.

499
00:39:52,807 --> 00:39:56,410
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it's like you're trying to train a dog with frustration.

500
00:39:57,311 --> 00:39:57,431
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

501
00:39:57,951 --> 00:40:02,856
[SPEAKER_03]: You're still saying the same things, doing the same thing, but your attitude is frustrated.

502
00:40:02,876 --> 00:40:05,679
[SPEAKER_03]: It's like, oh no, I gotta stop that first.

503
00:40:06,857 --> 00:40:11,059
[SPEAKER_03]: Defrustrate myself, unfrustrate myself, and then do the same things.

504
00:40:11,680 --> 00:40:17,943
[SPEAKER_03]: And though we get very different message in those two externally same-looking examples.

505
00:40:23,726 --> 00:40:27,368
[SPEAKER_03]: Now, you could see then all those similes in the suttas when it says, okay, his work is done.

506
00:40:29,008 --> 00:40:29,969
[SPEAKER_03]: Training's completed.

507
00:40:31,505 --> 00:40:35,267
[SPEAKER_03]: The elephant is completely immovable in the battle, or non-battle, doesn't matter.

508
00:40:36,148 --> 00:40:44,413
[SPEAKER_03]: So, the wild dog is completely tame now, cannot possibly bite you under any circumstance.

509
00:40:45,614 --> 00:40:47,295
[SPEAKER_03]: And you fully know that.

510
00:40:49,157 --> 00:40:58,503
[SPEAKER_03]: Because you were presented with scenarios, through the contemplation, the inevitabilities, that used to,

511
00:40:59,248 --> 00:41:01,949
[SPEAKER_03]: Cause agitation and threat and anxiety.

512
00:41:03,810 --> 00:41:04,651
[SPEAKER_03]: But now, it's none of that.

513
00:41:04,831 --> 00:41:10,373
[SPEAKER_03]: It's simply immovable and it looks looks at you with the same friendly eyes, so to speak, and you know it.

514
00:41:12,014 --> 00:41:12,574
[SPEAKER_03]: And you know that.

515
00:41:12,754 --> 00:41:21,899
[SPEAKER_03]: You know, like, you get a wild, crazy dog, you tame it, you train it, and it's like, you know, like, oh, that dog would give its life for me, basically.

516
00:41:21,919 --> 00:41:25,700
[SPEAKER_03]: There's nothing that can come in between, in that sense.

517
00:41:25,740 --> 00:41:28,482
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, it's exactly the same for the mind, if it's tamed.

518
00:41:29,629 --> 00:41:44,537
[SPEAKER_03]: So then, yeah, Arahant can literally go in any direction he pleases, towards any circumstances, and he'll be completely unbothered, because the root of the bother was the animal that's now incapable of that, incapable of craving.

